  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Do you want to study at a university that is known as The University of Opportunity?&nbsp;</p><p>A University that lives up to this reputation with its commitment to inclusion and diversity?</p><p>The University of Wolverhampton has been awarded four stars in the latest QS Stars international rating system for its international focus!</p><p>It offers over 250 undergraduate and 120 postgraduate courses, many of which are accredited by international professional bodies.</p><p>Over 40% of its students are over 25 years old on enrolment and its staff provide networks and resources to benefit gender, disability, race, and lifestyle.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Discover why University of Wolverhampton might just be the place for you!</strong></p><p style=\"text-align:center;\">&nbsp;<a href=\"https://edvoy.com/courses/?institutions=%5B%22University+of+Wolverhampton%22%5D&amp;fromInstitution=true&amp;locations=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22United+Kingdom%22%2C%22values%22%3A%5B%5D%7D%5D\">View courses now</a></p> <p>The University of Wolverhampton has invested in the development of its facilities over the past five years. New facilities include the Business School, state-of-the-art Rosalind Franklin Building and Springfield Campus, which is dedicated to architecture and built environment.</p> <p><strong>About the University</strong></p> <p>The University of Wolverhampton dates back to the Wolverhampton Tradesmenâ€™s and Mechanicsâ€™ Institute which was founded in 1827. In 1969 a merger with the Municipal School of Art created Wolverhampton Polytechnic and it gained university status in 1992. Its main campus is in the centre of Wolverhampton with additional campuses in Walsall and Telford.</p><p>It has over 21,000 students including around 2,500 international students from more than 130 nations. It has been ranked in the top 1000 global universities in the Times Higher Education World University Rankings. It has also been placed in the top 150 UK universities by The Guardian, The Times/Sunday Times and the Complete University Guide.</p> <p><strong>Why the University of Wolverhampton?</strong></p><p>The University of Wolverhampton has achieved fantastic rankings in accordance with several reputable sources.</p><p>The Daily Mail University Rankings and League Table 2024 ranked the university:</p><ul><li>Number 1 in the UK for teaching first-generation students. (i.e. the first in their family to go to university).</li><li>26th for Teaching Excellence&nbsp;</li><li>39th for Student Support</li></ul><p>Envision completing your educational path at the University of Wolverhampton, where you're imbued with vital skills, an expansive network, and the confidence to succeed in your career of choice.&nbsp;</p><p>Imagine the fulfillment that comes with obtaining a degree from an institution known for its outstanding achievements.</p><p>Picture the personal growth, freedom, and possibilities that are part of the university life experience.</p><p>Turn this envisioned scenario into your personal journey.</p><p>Step into the ranks of countless international students who have discovered their pathway to success at the University of Wolverhampton.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/courses/?institutions=%5B%22University+of+Wolverhampton%22%5D&amp;fromInstitution=true&amp;locations=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22United+Kingdom%22%2C%22values%22%3A%5B%5D%7D%5D\">Take a browse of the University of Wolverhampton today!</a></p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p><p>The university offers a comprehensive orientation program specifically tailored for international students, helping them acclimate to life in the UK and the university environment. This includes sessions on academic expectations, language support services, and cultural adaptation.</p><p>The University of Wolverhampton strives to create an inclusive and supportive environment for international students, encouraging them to engage fully with both the academic and social aspects of university life.</p>"
    ],
